{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1203 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "64136d2f9cd3043a74e18b943c5c39539f67ffb24c7443ce101d05031f5cbf49" :edb/db-before-t 1202 :edb/db-after-t 1203 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534515 50 #inst "2026-10-07T19:25:27.861Z" 13194139534515 true] [17592186096618 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292735 13194139534515 true] [17592186096619 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292742 13194139534515 true] [17592186096619 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292759 13194139534515 true] [17592186096620 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292749 13194139534515 true] [17592186096620 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292752 13194139534515 true] [17592186292735 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292736 13194139534515 true] [17592186292735 1089 "q-119044" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292735 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534515 true] [17592186292735 1100 "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-{2}^{x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292735 1113 #uuid "20cda5cd-39b4-5204-8a0d-778056eed590" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292735 1145 "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{2}^{x}.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{2}^{x})\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int {2}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{{2}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{{2}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int {2}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\frac{{2}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2})+Cx+D \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{x}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292736 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292737 13194139534515 true] [17592186292736 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292738 13194139534515 true] [17592186292736 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292739 13194139534515 true] [17592186292736 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292740 13194139534515 true] [17592186292736 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292741 13194139534515 true] [17592186292736 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534515 true] [17592186292736 1041 "selection" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292736 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292738 13194139534515 true] [17592186292736 1110 #uuid "e5356391-daef-5366-a605-c7b74b8f10e9" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292737 1034 "y={2}^{x}{ln}^{2}⁡2-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+Cx+D" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292737 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534515 true] [17592186292737 1111 #uuid "2710eb67-6841-5d5c-8e1e-039125c3b36d" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292738 1034 "y=\\frac{{2}^{x}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Cx+D" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292738 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534515 true] [17592186292738 1111 #uuid "c4048121-3fb2-5bcf-982e-cf851d1c607c" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292739 1034 "y=\\frac{{2}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Cx+D" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292739 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534515 true] [17592186292739 1111 #uuid "5af93b4d-1bd0-5e4d-ba64-e54d460cc6e3" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292740 1034 "y=\\frac{{2}^{x}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+Cx+D" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292740 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534515 true] [17592186292740 1111 #uuid "1ea0dc24-dc83-5857-a66e-00d0395664c5" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292741 1034 "y={2}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Cx+D" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292741 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534515 true] [17592186292741 1111 #uuid "c3ac503d-86b3-5bac-83b1-5ecf8f92865d" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292742 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292743 13194139534515 true] [17592186292742 1089 "q-119132" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292742 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534515 true] [17592186292742 1100 "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{e}^{-x/4}}{2}?$" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292742 1113 #uuid "370a4996-fe99-533f-b6a9-5042b61aa194" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292742 1145 "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{{e}^{-x/4}}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{-x/4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-4{e}^{-x/4}) \\\\  & =-2{e}^{-x/4}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=0,3,6.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/assets/a4b534bd33daabc94aa3c86935b1fd4c0be723fafbc418ed382716541a864293.png)" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292743 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292744 13194139534515 true] [17592186292743 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292745 13194139534515 true] [17592186292743 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292746 13194139534515 true] [17592186292743 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292747 13194139534515 true] [17592186292743 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292748 13194139534515 true] [17592186292743 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534515 true] [17592186292743 1041 "selection" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292743 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292744 13194139534515 true] [17592186292743 1110 #uuid "8d5b2ef1-c08b-50ea-a722-b5ebadbae937" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292744 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/assets/d7ecaa30c600519d6bfcc7a43a4275a55d6f6cc1b52b48c8e7b117e7a772343e.png" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292744 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534515 true] [17592186292744 1111 #uuid "fd7fb28d-d2af-5809-9602-c6c9c61aa684" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292745 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/assets/8ede6d26a62570f4037ecc58c377e95389ab00dbee36b60c46e6fb2021e01cea.png" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292745 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534515 true] [17592186292745 1111 #uuid "476b9b70-6126-5f8b-b65b-3ddd79e11fcc" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292746 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/assets/cece096a5b267821994e9b6d8142f0d7ea684bbe8e28da7cdb01b87a73f1db4c.png" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292746 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534515 true] [17592186292746 1111 #uuid "0252ec44-9753-55db-bbb2-be4dbfeaaa45" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292747 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/assets/96359fe35288b866cbf9fd929e2515af04a4ec0dc565a4cd4af9d3a8fcd20f94.png" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292747 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534515 true] [17592186292747 1111 #uuid "ae440fff-25e4-5f3f-841f-9ccae733397a" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292748 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/assets/7832a2110292cb364cf06c24eb51e9bb1ee42fe430ac8fcc381af047a09125e4.png" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292748 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534515 true] [17592186292748 1111 #uuid "4ccca60c-7f65-5eec-8bf7-fb08e7594b1d" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292749 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292750 13194139534515 true] [17592186292749 1089 "q-352066" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292749 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534515 true] [17592186292749 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $(x-3)^{2}{y}^{′}=8$ that satisfies the condition $y(4)=1.$\n\n$y=\\,${{field-1}}" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292749 1113 #uuid "d86030f5-75e2-57ba-94c6-7a636a2e8eeb" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292749 1145 "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{8}{(x-3)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {y}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{8}{(x-3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =8\\int \\frac{1}{(x-3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8(-\\frac{1}{x-3})+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{x-3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=-\\frac{8}{x-3}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(4)=1$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =-\\frac{8}{4-3}+C \\\\ 1 & =-8+C \\\\ C & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{8}{x-3}+9.\n$$" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292750 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292751 13194139534515 true] [17592186292750 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534515 true] [17592186292750 1041 "field-1" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292750 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292751 13194139534515 true] [17592186292750 1110 #uuid "fdaa6dac-352d-59d2-a0be-00d8b5580145" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292751 1034 "9-\\frac{8}{x-3}" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292751 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534515 true] [17592186292751 1111 #uuid "be185d95-e478-5395-97f2-47a81ca133e5" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292752 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292753 13194139534515 true] [17592186292752 1089 "q-50092" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292752 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534515 true] [17592186292752 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation below that satisfies the condition $y(1)=1.$\n\n$$\n2x+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{2}+4x.\n$$" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292752 1113 #uuid "ace322a0-7247-5b35-923e-e7ab39690f9e" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292752 1145 "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{2}+2x.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int ({x}^{2}+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+{x}^{2}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(1)=1$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+{x}^{2}+C \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{{1}^{3}}{3}+{1}^{2}+C \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{4}{3}+C \\\\ C & =-\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292753 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292754 13194139534515 true] [17592186292753 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292755 13194139534515 true] [17592186292753 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292756 13194139534515 true] [17592186292753 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292757 13194139534515 true] [17592186292753 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292758 13194139534515 true] [17592186292753 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534515 true] [17592186292753 1041 "selection" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292753 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292758 13194139534515 true] [17592186292753 1110 #uuid "4cc15847-4e8b-5777-a4fb-4e61736d2e6e" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292754 1034 "y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+2{x}^{2}-\\frac{4}{3}" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292754 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534515 true] [17592186292754 1111 #uuid "8e2bbd1a-d147-5327-8498-387d60664636" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292755 1034 "y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-{x}^{2}+\\frac{5}{3}" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292755 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534515 true] [17592186292755 1111 #uuid "51ab586d-13bb-5243-be67-501f24081fc4" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292756 1034 "y={x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-1" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292756 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534515 true] [17592186292756 1111 #uuid "ca7a2592-1d2c-59e3-8481-e9ee58933ff7" 13194139534515 true] [17592186292757 1034 "y={x}^{3}